<title>ZIMBABWE: Zimbabwe may import sugar in 1997, official says.</title>
<headline>Zimbabwe may import sugar in 1997, official says.</headline>
<dateline>HARARE 1996-12-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Zimbabwe may have to import sugar in 1997 to supplement a shortfall in stocks resulting from poor yields, a senior industry official said on Friday.</p>
<p>Zimbabwe Sugar Sales general manager David Rockliffe told reporters the poor harvest was largely due to late rains in 1995.</p>
<p>&quot;This current year production was disappointing, ending at 336,000 tonnes compared to 513,000 tonnes last year,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>He did not say how much sugar would be imported and from where. Zimbabwe normally produces an average of 500,000 tonnes of sugar annually. --Harare Newsroom +263-4 72 52 28/9</p>
